# Chosen-natural consumers of restricted cubic containment

The seed automizer supplies 11.2.2(1--4), short-block invariance supplies the
11.1.5 theta step, and the H-star intersection supplies the Hall--Cartan
step in 11.3.7. Each application preserves the original chosen module,
marked action, relative residuals and quotient maps. The independent
preceding-source inputs remain explicit with their existing producers.

These extensions remove the unrestricted cubic callback from this route;
they do not prove the unrestricted final assertion of source 11.0.4.
Import this module near the final consumers, separately from Preliminary,
since its applications depend on later local and shadow geometry.
Final chosen-natural assembly is owned by qt-d-1222-natural-local-geometry.
Source: Aschbacher--Smith, printed pp.760,765--768,773.
-/
